rec.games.hack's own dh07+@andrew.cmu.edu (David Hairston) said:
-some suggestions to make nethack3.0 more accessible:

		        [ ideas (most) deleted ]

Most of these ideas are bad; especially those about items not appearing on
the first levels.  I want *more* altars on the earlier level; I often never
find one until DL5 or so; and then it's likely as not (twice as likely as
not, actually) that it won't be of my alignment.

What's needed is for more beginners to use explore mode.

-explore-mode goes unused because it doesn't get your name up there in
-  lights, so perhaps explore-mode games could post scores with a clearly
-  labelled flag designating that progress as such. whether to post the
-  score or not should require confirmation. you should not be able to get
-  consultations in explore-mode.

Actually, a seperate explore list would be all that's really needed.  And
maybe a breakdown of how your score was determined when you died?

If people are complaining about the game being too hard, it should be
compiled without the HARD option set (and it's been hacked locally so that
you don't get an amulet of life saving this way).

In addition, the default news file should mention that Explore mode exists
and should be used by beginners to find out what things do, how things work.


